                <pb facs="0439" n="430" xml:id="pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/255: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-31T16:00:00-04:00">January 31, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Department’s telegram No. 10, January 22, 3 p.m. Foreign Office will accept
                    note as drafted with additional sentence as follows: “It is understood, however,
                    that if the ratification does not take place with[in] the period authorized by
                    law 5142 the <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> could be signed again so
                    as to continue in provisional effect.” Purpose is merely to harmonize formula of
                    the note with actual legal possibilities. Please instruct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
